{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner selects the proposed next bounded executor diagnostic within existing 484/9be: a test-only hook restricted to the one fixture object/life may observe the known ScopeObject waitUntil registrations while forwarding the exact original promise to the original native method with its original context. Record only pending/settled counts and fixed source labels per object life; retain no promises, fences, stores, native contexts, capabilities or exception/output text in the observation registry. It must not await a new condition, replace/cancel an original promise, add a registered native wait, change scheduling/control predicates or alter production wiring.\n\nTake the serializable snapshot after the already proven helper/pass cleanup and immediately before unchanged eviction. Read getAlarm only for the stated due-alarm hypothesis, retaining its actual value and distinguishing native time from the scripted fixture clock. Keep one existing focused witness, all assertions and the default timeout; preserve source checkpoints and original failure logs. No timeout/abort sweep, omitted restart block, gate, provider probe or new task is authorized. If the observer cannot be installed transparently at the pinned harness boundary, report that concrete limitation before running rather than inventing a native API.\n\nThis measures only the specific registered outer promises and observed alarm. A timed-out underlying RPC may outlive a settled dispatcher promise; zero counters prove neither all native handles are gone nor quiescence, old-release drain or provider exclusion. The full actual storage-preserving eviction/restart/no-original-resend proof remains owed. Use the result to locate the next source/harness dependency; do not treat observation as the executor ownership contract or activation evidence.","body":{"head":"7455501e80f074bcbd77a039264eb8e74b489375","limits":"Original native promise/context and witness/default timeout unchanged; no production or drain claim.","scope":"single test-only executor waitUntil/alarm observation"}}